# Doc history (preserve prior text with dates)

When you change `BACKLOG.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md`, or anything under `docs/`, do not
delete the previous fact. Keep it in the same file (or the file you moved
it to) with the date it was current. This is the **internal counterpart** of
`web/lib/changelog.ts` (user-facing UI). Do not put this history there.

## When to Keep History

- **Changing a number or estimate** (e.g., pricing from 90 → 68): Keep old value with date
- **Moving a section** (e.g., from BACKLOG to CHANGELOG): Copy in full; add History line noting origin
- **Evolving a design** (e.g., auth from magic-link → password): Keep old approach with date
- **Marking something done** (e.g., "Enchantment specialist (started)" → move to CHANGELOG): Remove from BACKLOG, keep in CHANGELOG History

## How to record a change

1. Leave the new current text at the top of the section.
2. Add or extend a `## History` section below (newest first).
3. Each block starts with the date the old text was true, then the old text.

Date format: `Sep 13, 2026` (same as the UI changelog). If you only know
when it was replaced, write `Until Sep 13, 2026`. Do not invent a start
date.

## Moving content between files

Copy the old section in full into the destination. Note where it lived and
until when. Replace the original with a one-line pointer plus a History
line that names the new path.

## Do not

- Overwrite a number, quota, estimate, or decision in place
- Summarize away an old table or sketch; keep the prior text
- Drop a section because it moved; the destination must include it

Good:

    ## History
    ### Until Sep 13, 2026
    Paid Claude pool was 90. Daily fuse was 200.

Bad:

    (delete the 90/200 paragraph and leave only 68/50)
